---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { buildBreadcrumbSchema, buildFAQSchema } from "../../lib/seo";

const pageFaqs = [
  {
    question: "How should I answer CELPIP Speaking Task 1?",
    answer: "Answer CELPIP Speaking Task 1 with a clear personal experience structure: context, key event, and takeaway. Keep the story simple and coherent.",
  },
  {
    question: "What is CELPIP Speaking Task 1 about?",
    answer: "CELPIP Speaking Task 1 usually asks you to describe a personal experience. You need to speak clearly, stay organized, and keep fluency under time pressure.",
  },
  {
    question: "What lowers CELPIP Task 1 speaking scores?",
    answer: "Scores drop when answers are disorganized, too short, repetitive, or filled with hesitation and filler words.",
  },
];

const pageStructuredData = [
  buildBreadcrumbSchema(Astro.site, [
    { name: "Home", path: "/" },
    { name: "Blog", path: "/blog/" },
    { name: "CELPIP Speaking Task 1", path: "/blog/celpip-speaking-task-1/" },
  ]),
  buildFAQSchema(pageFaqs),
];
---

<Layout
  title="CELPIP Speaking Task 1 | Personal Experience Structure Guide"
  description="CELPIP Speaking Task 1 strategy for personal-experience prompts, answer structure, fluency, and practical CLB 9 speaking habits."
  type="article"
  keywords="CELPIP Speaking Task 1, CELPIP speaking tips, CELPIP personal experience question, CLB 9 speaking"
  structuredData={pageStructuredData}
>
  <article class="section" style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; padding-top: var(--s-6);">
    <div style="margin-bottom: var(--s-4);"><a href="/blog" style="color: var(--accent);">← Back to blog</a></div>
    <header style="margin-bottom: var(--s-4);">
      <h1 style="margin: 0;">CELPIP Speaking Task 1 Guide</h1>
      <div style="display: flex; gap: var(--s-3); color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: var(--s-2); flex-wrap: wrap;">
        <span>📅 March 14, 2026</span><span>✍️ IELTS Corner Team</span><span>⏱️ 6 min read</span>
      </div>
    </header>
    <div class="article-content" style="line-height: 1.8;">
      <p>CELPIP Speaking Task 1 rewards clear storytelling, not dramatic language. A short, organized personal experience with one key message often performs better than a long, messy answer.</p>
      <h2>Simple Task 1 structure</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Context: where and when it happened</li>
        <li>Main event: what happened and why it mattered</li>
        <li>Outcome: what you learned or why it is memorable</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Fluency tips</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Use transition phrases: first, then, after that, finally</li>
        <li>Keep sentence length controlled under pressure</li>
        <li>Pause briefly instead of using many filler words</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Practice next</h2>
      <p>Use the <a href="/celpip/speaking">CELPIP speaking hub</a> and lesson pages like <a href="/lessons/speaking/celpip-task1-experience-b2/">Task 1 describe an experience</a>.</p>
      <h2>FAQ</h2>
      {pageFaqs.map((item) => (
        <details class="card" style="margin-bottom: var(--s-3);">
          <summary style="cursor: pointer; font-weight: 700;">{item.question}</summary>
          <p class="muted" style="margin-top: var(--s-2); margin-bottom: 0;">{item.answer}</p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>